# Environment Files - Stigmer Project
# Add this to your project's .gitignore

# =============================================================================
# Secret Files - NEVER COMMIT THESE
# =============================================================================

# Secret environment files
.env.secret
.env.secret.*
*.secret

# Local overrides (may contain secrets)
.env.local
.env.*.local

# =============================================================================
# Environment Files - Commit Based on Content
# =============================================================================

# If your .env contains secrets, add it here:
.env

# If your .env only has non-sensitive config, you can commit it.
# In that case, remove the line above and document which values
# are safe to commit in a comment.

# =============================================================================
# Example Template Files - SAFE TO COMMIT
# =============================================================================

# These should be committed as documentation:
# .env.example
# .env.secret.example
# README.md

# =============================================================================
# Usage Instructions
# =============================================================================
#
# 1. Copy the relevant lines to your project's .gitignore
#
# 2. Verify secrets are ignored:
#    git status
#    # .env.secret should NOT appear
#
# 3. Create template files for your team:
#    cp .env .env.example
#    # Edit .env.example to remove sensitive values
#    git add .env.example
#
# 4. Document setup in your README:
#    "Copy .env.example to .env and .env.secret.example to .env.secret,
#     then add your credentials."
#
# =============================================================================
# Verification
# =============================================================================
#
# Check if .env.secret is properly ignored:
#   echo "TEST_SECRET=value" > .env.secret
#   git status
#   # Should NOT show .env.secret as untracked
#
# If .env.secret appears in git status, add it to .gitignore!
#
